# Who has to look at what.
#
# The point of this file is narrow and specific: twelve agents writing in
# parallel is only safe if the files they all depend on cannot be changed
# quietly. Those files are the contracts and the gates.
#
# GitHub only *requests* a review from these owners. To make it blocking, turn
# on "Require review from Code Owners" in Settings -> Branches. Without that,
# this file is a suggestion; with it, it is the mechanism that makes the frozen
# API meaningful.

# --- The frozen public API of :core -----------------------------------------
# Changing this file IS changing the contract every other workstream codes
# against. It must be a deliberate, reviewed act, never a side effect of a
# refactor.
core/api/core.api @riceharvest

# --- The gates themselves ---------------------------------------------------
# Someone can always edit the check that was failing them. That is why these are
# owned separately from the code they police.
scripts/ @riceharvest
.github/workflows/ @riceharvest
ci/ @riceharvest

# --- Build configuration ---------------------------------------------------
# Dependency policy lives in the catalog; a change here changes what the whole
# app links against.
gradle/libs.versions.toml @riceharvest
settings.gradle.kts @riceharvest
build.gradle.kts @riceharvest
**/build.gradle.kts @riceharvest

# --- Documentation that defines the rules ----------------------------------
docs/architecture.md @riceharvest
docs/swarm-plan.md @riceharvest
docs/evals.md @riceharvest
